WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.517
Microsoft Fabric has more than one place where S Q L can appear, so always check which engine is running your code.

00:00:07.517 --> 00:00:12.472
A Spark notebook or Spark S Q L cell runs through Spark.

00:00:12.472 --> 00:00:21.124
A Fabric S Q L analytics endpoint uses a different S Q L serving environment and often follows T S Q L conventions.

00:00:21.596 --> 00:00:29.293
The same query concept may therefore need slightly different syntax depending on the surface.

00:00:29.293 --> 00:00:33.213
When code fails, do not immediately assume the analytical idea is wrong.

00:00:33.213 --> 00:00:40.001
First ask: which engine am I using, and which S Q L dialect does that engine expect?
